---
id: org.dxos.plugin.sensemaking
name: SensemakingPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Sensemaking is the horizontal **Workbench** layer over Composer. Its first increment is the
**Inbox**: captures — items Steve flagged from any source (fed today by `plugin-readwise`'s Readwise
highlights) — land here, grouped by the document they came from, where Steve manually triages each
into **results** (to-dos, questions) or **connects** it to a project, with every result traceable
back to the capture it came from.

This is the first increment of the Workbench arc (see
`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-workbench-concept.md`); later increments add the Pipeline (tracked
work) and AI-assisted triage, and more sources feeding the same Inbox. The plugin owns two ECHO types
— `Capture` (the source-agnostic envelope) and `Result` — plus two relations (`DerivedFrom` for
traceability, `ConnectedTo` for connect); it composes `Collection` (as connect targets) and renders
each capture's source item via that source's own card, so the Inbox stays source-agnostic.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0`         |

## Types

```mdl
type Capture
  desc: |
    The source-agnostic envelope: an item Steve flagged, where it came from, and his optional
    note/tags. `source` is the flagged item itself (a reading highlight today); `referent` is the
    document it belongs to, used to cluster the Inbox; `flaggedAt` orders the Inbox.
  fields:
    source: Ref<any>          # the flagged source item
    referent?: Ref<any>       # the document it belongs to (clusters the Inbox)
    flaggedAt: string         # ISO timestamp; orders the Inbox
    note?: string
    tags?: string[]
```

```mdl
type Result
  desc: One triage outcome derived from a capture.
  fields:
    kind: todo | question
    body: string
```

## Relations

```mdl
type DerivedFrom
  desc: Traceability relation, source → target = Result → the Capture it was derived from. Every result stays reachable from its origin capture.
```

```mdl
type ConnectedTo
  desc: Connect relation, source → target = Capture → the object it belongs with (a project Collection today, any object in principle).
```

## Operations

```mdl
op SensemakingOperation.CreateResult
  desc: |
    Creates a triage Result (to-do or question) from a capture and records a DerivedFrom relation
    from the result back to the capture, so the result is always traceable to its origin.
  input:
    capture: Ref<Capture>
    kind: todo | question
    body: string
  output:
    result: Ref<Result>
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SensemakingOperation.Connect
  desc: Connects a capture to a target object (a project Collection today) via a ConnectedTo relation.
  input:
    capture: Ref<Capture>
    target: Ref<any>
  effects: [echo:write]
```

## Components

```mdl
component Inbox
  desc: |
    The Inbox article surface for a space. Groups the space's captures under the source document
    they came from, most-recently-active document first, and renders each capture with its triage
    controls. Appears in the space navigation only when the space has at least one capture.
  props:
    space: Space
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ N captures                                   │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ ┌ The Great Reorg · Azeem Azhar · 3  [↗]  ┐ │
    │ │  ● source · see in source ↗              │ │
    │ │  ▍ passage                               │ │
    │ │  ✎ note                                  │ │
    │ │  YOUR RESULTS                            │ │
    │ │   ✓ a to-do    ↳ from this capture   ✕   │ │
    │ │  [+ result ▾]                            │ │
    │ │ ┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈ │ │
    │ │  ● source · see in source ↗              │ │
    │ │  ▍ passage …                             │ │
    │ └──────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
    └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component CaptureRow
  desc: |
    One capture within the Inbox: its source item rendered inline via that source's own card, a
    source-tag with a link to the item's origin, an inline list of the capture's results (each
    labelled as derived from this capture and individually removable), and a "+ result" control to
    add a to-do / question or connect the capture to a project. Aligned in a single body column so
    the source card, results, and controls share one left edge.
  props:
    capture: Capture
    space: Space
  actions:
    addResult(kind) → Result
    connect(target)
    removeResult(result)
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Inbox

  req F-1.1:
    given: a space whose sources have produced at least one capture
    when: the user opens the space
    then: an "Inbox" appears in the space navigation
    and: a space with no captures shows no Inbox

  req F-1.2:
    given: an Inbox holding captures from one or more source documents
    when: the user views it
    then: captures are grouped under the source document they were captured from
    and: each group is labelled with the document's title and its capture count
    and: groups with more-recent activity appear first

  req F-1.3:
    given: a capture in the Inbox
    when: the user views it
    then: the captured item is shown inline (for a reading highlight: its passage, the note when present, and tags)
    and: the capture is labelled with the source it came from
    and: a link opens the item at its origin
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Triage into results

  req F-2.1:
    given: a capture in the Inbox
    when: the user adds a to-do or a question from the capture's "+ result" control
    then: the result is created and listed under the capture
    and: the result records the capture it was derived from

  req F-2.2:
    given: a capture with one or more results
    when: the user views it
    then: each result shows its kind (to-do or question) and its text
    and: each result shows that it was derived from this capture

  req F-2.3:
    given: a result listed under a capture
    when: the user removes it
    then: the result no longer appears under the capture
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Connect

  req F-3.1:
    given: a capture in the Inbox and one or more projects in the space
    when: the user connects the capture to a project from the "+ result" control
    then: a connection is recorded from the capture to that project

  req F-3.2:
    given: a space with no projects
    when: the user opens the connect options in the "+ result" control
    then: the control indicates there are no projects to connect to
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Triage creates a result traceable to its capture
  desc: Automated — src/operations/triage.test.ts, src/types/relations.test.ts, src/types/Result.test.ts.
  given: a capture
  when: a to-do result is created from it
  then:
    - the result is persisted with its kind and body
    - the result is reachable from the capture via the DerivedFrom relation
```

```mdl
test T-2: Connect records a relation from the capture to the target
  desc: Automated — src/operations/triage.test.ts, src/types/relations.test.ts.
  given: a capture and a target object
  when: the capture is connected to the target
  then: a ConnectedTo relation exists from the capture to the target
```

```mdl
test T-3: Captures cluster by source, most-recent first
  desc: Automated — src/operations/cluster.test.ts.
  given: captures spanning several source documents flagged at different times
  when: the Inbox clustering is computed
  then:
    - captures are grouped by their source document
    - the groups are ordered by their most recent flag time, newest first
```

```mdl
test T-4: The plugin registers its types on startup
  desc: Automated — src/SensemakingPlugin.test.ts.
  given: the plugin is enabled in a test app
  when: it starts up
  then: its schema module activates and registers the Capture type
```

```mdl
test T-5: Walking-skeleton acceptance — capture, triage, connect, verified against the mockup
  desc: |
    Covered by a live manual acceptance run against a running Composer, computed-style-verified with
    the `visual-verification` skill (.agents/skills/visual-verification), not a unit test.
  given: a space fed by a connected source (Readwise), with synced captures
  when: the user opens the Inbox and triages a capture
  then:
    - the Inbox appears in navigation once the space has captures
    - captures are grouped by source document, most-recently-active first
    - each capture shows its source item inline with a link to its origin
    - adding a to-do / question lists it under the capture, marked as derived from it
    - removing a result drops it from the capture
    - connecting a capture to a project records the connection
    - the rendered Inbox matches the Workbench mockup on every measured property (per the
      visual-verification differ), residual differences being deliberate design-token / platform
      choices only
```

